.TH FUSEGL 1 "October 2026" "FuseGL" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fusegl \- compile FuseGL source to a GLSL fragment shader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fusegl
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B fusegl
[\fB--builtins\fR]
.br
.B fusegl lsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fusegl
reads one FuseGL program from standard input and writes a GLSL 330 fragment
shader to standard output. It is deliberately a filter, so it can be used
alone or as part of a build pipeline.
.PP
The generated shader expects the host to provide the
.B matterboxUv
texture coordinate. It also expects \fBu_time\fR and \fBu_resolution\fR
uniforms and any used texture inputs \fBtex0\fR through \fBtex3\fR.
The existing input name is retained for compatibility with legacy hosts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lsp
Run the FuseGL language server over JSON-RPC on standard input and output.
It provides diagnostics, receiver-aware completion, and hover documentation
using the same shader catalog as compilation and \fB--builtins\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --preview-line " N"
Compile the intermediate result selected by source line \fIN\fR. The result
must be a previewable numeric or vector value.
.TP
.B --builtins
Print all FuseGL function signatures, globals, and their descriptions.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a short usage guide.
.SH LANGUAGE API
FuseGL uses dot calls for pipeline stages. The value on the left is passed as
the first argument to the next function. Regular calls are also available for
constructors and functions with additional arguments.
.PP
.nf
sample(vec2, texture) -> vec4
scroll(vec2, vec2, float) -> vec2
repeat(vec2) -> vec2
mirror(vec2) -> vec2
mirror(vec2, texture) -> vec2
zoom(vec2, float) -> vec2
distort(vec2, vec4, float) -> vec2
r(vec4) -> float       g(vec4) -> float
b(vec4) -> float       a(vec4) -> float
clamp(float, float, float) -> float
vec2(float, float) -> vec2
vec3(float, float, float) -> vec3
vec4(vec2, float, float) -> vec4
vec4(vec3, float) -> vec4
vec4(float, float, float, float) -> vec4
center(vec2) -> vec2    aspect(vec2) -> vec2
rotate(vec2, float) -> vec2
oscillate(float, float, float) -> float
cycle(float, float, float, float) -> float
radial_wave(vec2, float, float, float) -> float
circle(vec2, float) -> float
box(vec2, vec2) -> float
sdf_union(float, float) -> float
fill(float) -> float     stroke(float, float) -> float
rgb(float, float, float) -> vec3
colorize(float, vec3) -> vec4
add(float, float) -> float
blend_add(vec4, vec4) -> vec4
multiply(float, float) -> float
multiply(vec4, vec4) -> vec4
.fi
.PP
.B uv
is the normalized fragment coordinate. \fBresolution\fR is the output size
in pixels, \fBtime\fR is elapsed animation time, and \fBtex0\fR through
\fBtex3\fR are configured texture inputs.
.PP
Use \fBfusegl --builtins\fR for the complete descriptions of these functions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fusegl < main.pgl > main.frag
fusegl --preview-line 4 < main.pgl > preview.frag
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and non-zero for invalid options, source, or output.
